{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>Please.</b> Like \"now,\" and so every נא in Scripture; it is the reverse in the language of Ishmael." "<b>For therefore you know.</b> Like \"for therefore I did not give her to Shelah.\" The meaning: since you know our encampments — that you know the place where we camped there." "<b>Come with us and you will be for us as eyes.</b> To show the way. And many say that והיית is past tense, alluding to the counsel he gave Moses, for he showed him what he did not know; and this is the meaning of \"as eyes.\"" "And the meaning of <b>And he said, Please.</b> He had already said the like to him, but it did not help."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:17:04.765967141Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}